# Nb - Ugur interatomic potential, switched, with the angular factor
#
# pair_style ugur/ang
# pair_coeff * * Nb_taper.ugur.ang Nb
#
# Truncation: switched from 0.85 of each cutoff to the cutoff, quintic, C2 - energy is conserved in MD
# MD: SUSPECT.  At 600 K this runs at 473 K where equipartition gives 300; something is releasing energy.  Check before trusting it.
#
# Nudge test: FAILED.  Displace every atom by 1e-5 A and relax, and the crystal keeps 13857x that displacement and settles 1.28 meV/atom LOWER.  The reference lattice is not this potential's minimum, so the elastic constants above are the constants of a structure it does not hold.  Static reference only; do not use for defects, surfaces or dynamics.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Nb at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
